<title>CANADA: NOVA Q4 shr net rises after writedown.</title>
<headline>NOVA Q4 shr net rises after writedown.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			 1995</p>
<p> Shr			 C$0.23		   C$0.19</p>
<p> Net			108,000		   89,000</p>
<p> Revs		   1,191,000		1,073,000</p>
<p>				YEAR</p>
<p> Shr			 C$0.91		   C$1.44</p>
<p> Net			431,000		  702,000</p>
<p> Revs		   4,686,000		4,527,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 475,000		  479,000</p>
<p>	(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: NOVA Corp's share of a writedown announced by 25-percent owned Methanex Corp, made after capacity was reduced at higher-cost methanol facilities, was C$32 million, resulting in a 1996 fourth-quarter loss of C$23 million.</p>
<p>Net income per share before the writedown was C$0.30 in the fourth quarter of 1996 and C$0.98 for the full year.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
